A||N||14||Jay||Supercharging Northstar||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||09-28-2001||05:29 PM||||An idea I've been throwing around for a  while...Supercharge the Northstar.  A supercharger could probably fit where the A/C compressor or even the powersteering pump used to be.  The only thing is, I don't know which blower to go with and what internal engine mods should be done.  Anyone ever consider this?  JM I know you have, how about Will or Artherd?<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||09-28-2001||05:36 PM||||Here's a link to a site I ran across where the guy is trying to get a group order for a SC kit to go on a Northstar in a Cadillac. Might be of some help...<P> <A HREF="http://web2.airmail.net/nunnally/sts/northstarsupercharger.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://web2.airmail.net/nunnally/sts/northstarsupercharger.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||09-28-2001||05:40 PM||||I'm gonna check them out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||09-28-2001||06:51 PM||||Jay you will have to go custom.  I would go with a Paxton unit.  Reliable supercharger.  I would call them, tell them what engine you have, how much boost you want to run, and your compression ratio.  You will need the blower only.  Ask them if they have something compact but yet can be attached inline with your accesories without too much hassle.  I am sure they have a supercharger to suit your needs.  I would go no more then 5-6 psi to start with of course and go from there.  <P>You will have to do all the plumbing yourself which isn't that hard unless there just is no room, and the fuel delivery mods or reprogram the ecm somehow to get more fuel in.  Or a rising rate FPR would work.  Timing could probably be handled by a aftermarket ignition with a boost timing control module like Crane or MSD.  A 2 bar map will need to be used as well.<P>I would like to see this done.  I think it would smoke some butt and noone else would have what you have.  <P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||09-28-2001||07:01 PM||||Get a blower for a 4.6ltr mustang.<P>Get a electromotvie Tec system <BR>Get a electromotvie Tec system <BR>Get a electromotvie Tec system <P><BR>Around $1500 Canadian , But sooooo worth it. I just got turned onto these by friends running Datsun 240's . 3.0ltr inline 6 , no turbo putting out 260 @ the wheels , and street driven.<P>I would toss all ideas of getting a chip burned and get one of these units. Get the Electromotvie unit and you can tune the car to the Nth degree.<P>I have looked at a few N*'s , ducting the  tube into the TB is the real engineering feat , doesn't seem t be much room in a Fiero to run it easily.<P>but anything can be done with a little inginuity (sp?)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-28-2001||11:56 PM||||Hi Jay, a Paxton centrifugical unit running low-ish boost, ie 4-5lbs max. (hint: think about one for a 4.6litre mustang  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>This should be good for roughly another ~80-100bhp peak (!!!)  <P>You're using the stock ECU right?  Might be time to consider the 950 Commander aftermarket unit (with this, you're basically a GM engineer and can change *anything* including but not limited to: ignition timing, full 3d map fuel delivery, sweet engine mojo level....)  <P>The above will be an absolute necessity if you want to go over very mild boost levels.  <P>I don't think any internal mods would really be nessicary, the stock internals are pretty strong.<P>The next step up would be a big one, custom machined steel cranks and fordged (Ti?) rods, etc.<P>There's also <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>www.chrfab.com</A>  heads to be considered (nearly +100bhp with their midrange cam, all on atmosphere, and an increase in redline to around 7500-8k <BR>with solid lifters...)<P><BR>Keep us all apprised on what you do!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||Joe Torma||09-29-2001||02:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Get a blower for a 4.6ltr mustang.<P>Get a electromotvie Tec system <BR>Get a electromotvie Tec system <BR>Get a electromotvie Tec system <P><BR>Around $1500 Canadian , But sooooo worth it. I just got turned onto these by friends running Datsun 240's . 3.0ltr inline 6 , no turbo putting out 260 @ the wheels , and street driven.<P>I would toss all ideas of getting a chip burned and get one of these units. Get the Electromotvie unit and you can tune the car to the Nth degree.<P>I have looked at a few N*'s , ducting the  tube into the TB is the real engineering feat , doesn't seem t be much room in a Fiero to run it easily.<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yup, I recommend it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Incredible system...now if only I could get mine(3400+TEC) to idle right.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>Did you guys see a picture of the Caddy V12...WOW!!!  Over 700 HP?! Sick.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
