Z||000009||Shaun41178||09-30-2001||01:18 PM||||Jay for the price of the blower and the headache of trying to get teh plumbing setup,I would just go with the CHRfab detup.  Go with the heads and new cam package they offer.  For around $2200 you can get around a 75 hp gain or so.  Which is what you would probably see with a supercharger but much less headache.  While it is apart, gasket match the intake manifolds and even if you want send them out to be extrude honed.  Thats costly but you will pick up some more ponies too.  But for about $2200 US dollars you can have close to 400 ponies under your hood.  And 7k rpm redline too!  hehe.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jay||09-30-2001||06:13 PM||||Shaun, I agree but $2200 US is like a Billion  Canadian right now <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If we could get the specs on the cams I could get someone to machine them here in Toronto for a lot cheaper.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Shaun41178||09-30-2001||06:57 PM||||Jay call them up and ask them.  I am sure they would tell you the specs on the cams they sell.  Andfind out what the stock ones are too if you don't know.  Just act like you want to spend a ton of money with them and I am sure they will answer all your questions.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||10-01-2001||01:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B>While it is apart, gasket match the intake manifolds and even if you want send them out to be extrude honed.  Thats costly but you will pick up some more ponies too. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Shaun, while I stand behind your recomendation to get the chrfab parts, I do have to point out that you can't 'extrude hone' the Northstar's intake manifold...<P>as it dosen't really have one.<P>Instead it has what are essentially a bunch of velocity stack horns (cast in plastic resin, not aluminum) that are curved in on each other inside a common airbox...<P>...and that's it!<P>Kinda cool actually.  and the *whole* intake weighs about 10lbs. (and is a one piece unit that bolts directly to the cyl heads)<P>It's a thousand times better than the 'design' of the 2.8 for example.  I find it amazingly easy to work on, and really well thought out.  the 2.8 on the other hand...<P>(it's basically what you'd expect when going from adaptations of 60+ year old designs to starting with a totally clean sheet of paper.)<P>I still can't belive it bolts up to the Fiero trannys, how cool is that?!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||Shaun41178||10-01-2001||01:13 PM||||Thanks for the correction Arther.  Sorry if I misinformed anyone out there.<P>Hehe well just extrude hone the heads then??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||10-01-2001||03:29 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/chevv8.jpg"> <P>Yummy...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.twminduction.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twminduction.com</A> <P>From the sounds of it , a system like this on the N* wouldn't be too difficult.<P>Looks exotic , Ferrari like ..and I know you like Ferrari's Jay.<P>This setup is for a V8 Chev.<P>JM||||reg||1
